      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>form 990, part I, line 1, description of organization mission:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>TO PROVIDE HEALTH BENEFITS, TERM LIFE AND ACCIDENTAL DEATH AND DISMEMBERMENT COVERAGE BENEFITS FOR ELIGIBLE ACTIVE PARTICIPANTS THROUGH A MULTI-EMPLOYER TRUST FUND.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, part iii, line 1, description of organization mission:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>TO PROVIDE HEALTH BENEFITS, TERM LIFE AND ACCIDENTAL DEATH AND DISMEMBERMENT OVERAGE BENEFITS FOR ELIGIBLE ACTIVE PARTICIPANTS THROUGH A Multi-employer trust fund. In addition, the plan offers medical and prescription drug plan options for eligible retiree participants and spouses, as well as a health reimbursement (hra) to active employees, retired employees, and former employees for whom employer contributions were made to individual accounts after October 1, 2012. The plan is maintained in compliance with the provisions of the employee retirement income security act of 1974, as amended (erisa).</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART III, LINE 1:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>the organization is a voluntary employee benefit plan with 100% of its activity and purpose relating to offering medical, prescription drug, dental, vision, term life and accidental death and dismemberment coverage benefits for eligible active participants.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, part vi, section a, line 8b:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The organization has no other committees.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, part vi, section b, line 11b:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Trustees review form 990 after the contract administrator has reviewed the form and compared it to the audited financial statements.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, part vi, section b, line 12c:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Section vi, 19 of the trust agreement outlines the conflict of interest policy. The trustees annually review their compliance with the guidelines of section 4975 irc and section 406 of erisa.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, part vi, section c, line 19:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The trust makes its governing documents, conflict of interest policy, and financial statements available to the participating employers and trust participants upon request.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
